# {{lb|en|originally|US|informal|derogatory}} [[meek|Meek]], [[timid]]; [[lack#Verb|lacking]] [[character]] or [[effectiveness]].
#: {{synonyms|en|feeble|ineffectual|insipid}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|speaker=[[w:Donald W. Nicholson|Donald W[illiam] Nicholson]]|quotee=[[w:Joseph W. Martin Jr.|Joseph W[illiam] Martin Jr.]]|debate=Extension of Remarks of Donald W. Nicholson of Massachusetts in the House of Representatives|report=[[w:Congressional Record|Congressional Record: Proceedings and Debates of the 82d Congress, First Session: Appendix]]|house={{w|United States House of Representatives}}|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|United States Government Printing Office]]|date=29 July 1951|year_published=31 July 1951|volume=97, part 14|page=A4814|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=oLJ6Q98c4hIC&pg=SL1-PA4814|column=1|issn=0363-7239|oclc=13530005|passage=The truth is that we are cursed with a "'''milquetoast'''" Government operating under "'''milquetoast'''" policies. Fear has become a national policy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Edward C[hristie] Banfield|authorlink=Edward C. Banfield|chapter=The Mythology of Influence|title=Political Influence|location=Glencoe, Ill.|publisher=[[w:Free Press (publisher)|Free Press of Glencoe]]|year=1961|oclc=933952628|location2=New Brunswick, N.J.; London|publisher2={{w|Transaction Publishers}}|year2=2003 (2009 printing)|page2=302|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=OziyfCcmVyYC&pg=PA302|isbn2=978-0-7658-0556-0|passage=If Bach had any guts, he wouldn't take that. He's too much of a '''Milquetoast''' guy.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=William G. Lycan|authorlink=William Lycan|chapter=Fiction and Essence|title=Modality and Meaning|location=Dordrecht|publisher=[[w:Springer Science+Business Media|Kluwer Academic Publishers]]|year=1994|section=section 4 (The Modal Properties of Fictional Individuals)|page=115|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZvSrR8OUlWgC&pg=PA115|isbn=978-0-7923-3006-6|passage=I should have listened to my mother when she told me to stay out of journalism because of idiot '''milquetoast''' jerk reporters like you!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Barry Gifford|authorlink=Barry Gifford|chapter=[[w:The Getaway (1972 film)|The Getaway]]|title=Out of the Past: Adventures in Film Noir|edition=revised|location=Jackson, Miss.|publisher={{w|University Press of Mississippi}}|year=2001|page=68|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=YTpaSviWrzIC&pg=PA68|isbn=978-1-57806-290-4|passage=[[w:Al Lettieri|[Al] Lettieri]] turns [[w:Sally Struthers|[Sally] Struthers]] on and she strokes his big gun and waves it (and her big tits) in his face and flaunts her partiality for the tough thug Lettieri over her '''milquetoast''' husband.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Rosemond|authorlink=John Rosemond|chapter=Command, Compel, Confirm|editor=Mary McNeil|title=Parenting by the Book: Biblical Wisdom for Raising Your Child|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Howard Books}}|year=2007|section=part 3 (Discipline)|page=239|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-7f71p0BJUkC&pg=PA239|isbn=978-1-4165-4484-5|passage=Like that well-meaning mom, parents employ '''Milquetoast''' speech whenever they whine, complain, plead, entreat, entice, bribe, and explain themselves persuasively.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Gerard DeGroot|chapter=Meet the New Boss|title=The 60s Unplugged: A Kaleidoscopic History of a Disorderly Decade|location=London|publisher=[[w:Macmillan Publishers|Macmillan]]|year=2008|isbn=978-1-4050-5521-5|edition2=paperback|location2=London|publisher2={{w|Pan Books}}|year2=2009|page2=393|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=Aa8qAIhxIO4C&pg=PA393|isbn2=978-0-330-44172-8|passage=[[w:Ricky Nelson|Ricky [Nelson]]] was the perfect commodity: an artist who did not upset '''milktoast''' America. He was [[w:Elvis Presley|Elvis [Presley]]] without grease, without swinging hips.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Christopher Kelly|authorlink=Christopher Kelly (author)|title=The Pink Bus|location=Mapple Shade, N.J.|publisher={{w|Lethe Press}}|year=2016|page=80|isbn=978-1-59021-495-4|passage=And if Dick Leonard didn't appreciate Patrick's incisive criticism—if it inspired a streak of vindictiveness in his usually '''milquetoast''' boss and Dick ended up making his assistant's life miserable?}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=David Ehrlich|title=‘Eva’ Review: Not Even {{w|Isabelle Huppert}} Playing an Irritated Prostitute Can Save this Limp Melodrama|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190416044058/https://www.indiewire.com/2018/02/eva-review-benoit-jacquot-isabelle-huppert-1201930011/|archivedate=16 April 2019|work={{w|IndieWire}}|date=18 February 2018|passage=Moreover, "[[w:Eva (2018 film)|Eva]]" boasts little style beyond what its biggest star is able to bring to the table. Viewers hoping for more of the '''milquetoast''' elegance that [[w:Benoît Jacquot|[Benoît] Jacquot]] previously brought to the likes of "{{w|Farewell, My Queen}}" and "[[w:Diary of a Chambermaid (2015 film)|Diary of a Chambermaid]]" will be disappointed.}}

